---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';   // the same rows and the same card treatment as the index
import '../styles/about.css';
import portrait from '../assets/img/about-portrait.png';
import sketch1 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-1.png';
import sketch2 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-2.png';
import studio1 from '../assets/img/about-studio-1.png';
import studio2 from '../assets/img/about-studio-2.png';
import home1 from '../assets/img/about-home-1.png';
import home2 from '../assets/img/about-home-2.png';
import michigan from '../assets/img/about-michigan.jpg';

// The same eight pictures the Webflow About page used, framed like the project cards on the
// index: 24px radius, no hairline, the image covering the frame. Each is sized by what it is —
// the portrait full width at its own 3:2; in a chapter, the author small under the date
// (columns 1–3) and the place under the words (6–12) at its own proportion, or the street across
// all twelve; the group photo small under its date, the last chapter standing on its text.
// No hairline in the body: sections are parted by air and by the change of scale.
const wide = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1600, 2036], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 92vw, 1248px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const column = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1440, 2048], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 84vw, (max-width: 1440px) 50vw, 718px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const small = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [480, 800, 1200], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 42vw, (max-width: 1440px) 21vw, 294px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };

const facts = [
  { label: 'Worked with', items: ['Temper', 'Dify (LangGenius)', 'Curio Digital Therapeutics', 'Infloww', 'Heygen', 'Eaton Corporation'] },
  { label: 'Also with', items: ["Xi'an University of Architecture and Technology", 'HIL Architects', 'ColdMe', 'COIL Connect for Virtual Exchange', 'Capital Area District Libraries', 'Erb Family Foundation'] },
  { label: 'Skills', items: ['AI UX', 'Agent workflows', 'Design systems', 'Design-to-code', 'Frontend prototyping', 'Design ops', 'Information architecture', 'Product strategy', 'UX research', 'Usability testing'] },
  { label: 'Tools', items: ['Figma', 'Claude Code', 'Cursor', 'Codex', 'React', 'TypeScript', 'Tailwind', 'HTML / CSS', 'JavaScript', 'Vitest', 'Python'] },
  { label: 'Languages', items: ['English', 'Mandarin (native)'] },
];
---
<Sheet
  title="About — Kyle Xu"
  description="Kyle Xu, AI product designer. Trained as an architect, then in HCI at the University of Michigan; since 2022 at Eaton, Heygen, Infloww, Curio Digital Therapeutics, Dify and Temper."
  ogImage="/og-about.jpg"
>
  <section class="col hero" aria-labelledby="h1">
    <h1 class="display" id="h1">At fifteen I was sketching buildings instead of studying for the gaokao.</h1>
    <p class="lead deck">Product designer for AI systems, trained as an architect.</p>
    <p class="lead">Xi'an, then a master's in HCI at the University of Michigan. Enterprise tools and AI products since 2022, most recently on contract at Temper.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="Portrait">
    <div class="photo"><Picture src={portrait} {...wide} loading="eager" alt="Kyle in kendo uniform, holding a helmet, in front of a wall of labelled equipment shelves" /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="Organisations, skills, tools and languages">
    <dl class="facts">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="meta">{f.label}</dt>
          <dd>{f.items.map((it, i) => <><span class="nb">{it}{i < f.items.length - 1 && ','}</span>{i < f.items.length - 1 && ' '}</>)}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="How I got here">
    <ul class="tl story">
      <li>
        <div class="side">
          <span class="meta when">2013 – 2018</span>
          <div class="photo me"><Picture src={sketch1} {...small} alt="Kyle as a student, sitting on the steps of a rooftop garden" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <h2>Workshops in Hangzhou, a studio at eighteen</h2>
          <p>In 2013, at fifteen, I was in volunteer building workshops in Hangzhou, making small physical improvements for people the city had overlooked. By 2017 I was designing spaces and art pieces for my father's business associates, and the hobby paid for itself. At eighteen a local design studio took me on for my first professional project.</p>
          <div class="photo place pano"><Picture src={studio1} {...column} alt="A small studio interior: a long wooden table and a glass partition" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="side">
          <span class="meta when">2019</span>
          <div class="photo me"><Picture src={sketch2} {...small} alt="Kyle's reflection in the window of a brick building, camera raised" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <h2>A year at an <span class="nb">urban-design</span> practice</h2>
          <p>In 2019 I worked part-time as a junior architect at an <span class="nb">urban-design</span> practice, and learned that cost and construction decide more of a building than the drawing does. Outside the field nobody wanted a junior architect, so I found my own clients while still a student.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="photo place pano full"><Picture src={studio2} {...wide} alt="A narrow city street lined with shop signs" /></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="side">
          <span class="meta when">2020 – 2022</span>
          <div class="photo me up"><Picture src={home1} {...small} alt="Kyle at a workbench in a workshop" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <h2>Three years at home</h2>
          <p>From 2020 I worked from home. There were UI and UX projects with partners in several Chinese cities, and a digital platform for a community in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, a joint project between my university and the city. The one I remember best is the app a few of us from a film community built and launched in a stretch of long days.</p>
          <div class="photo place up"><Picture src={home2} {...column} alt="A night-market kitchen in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, cooks at the grills" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="side">
          <span class="meta when">2022 – 2025</span>
          <div class="photo me"><Picture src={michigan} {...small} alt="Kyle with classmates at the University of Michigan" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <h2>Eaton, Michigan, and the first AI products</h2>
          <p>In 2022 I interned at Eaton on an IoT configuration tool for airport clients, then began a master's in HCI at the University of Michigan. At Heygen I <span class="nb">re-architected</span> the AI video editor around the script. At Infloww I designed a chat assistant for a B2B CRM and, with the prompt engineers, the payment and messaging tools around it, for the cases where the model is wrong. At Curio Digital Therapeutics I was the founding product designer on MamaLift and MenoLift, two <span class="nb">FDA-cleared</span> products; the design system, the information architecture and the Achievement Garden all went through clinical review.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="meta when">2026</span>
        <div class="what">
          <h2>Three products at Dify, and Temper's codebase</h2>
          <p>At Dify, an AI application platform, I designed three products: Droploft, a team knowledge base; Syncless, a <span class="nb">multi-agent</span> workplace concept; and Skills Agent, for Dify Enterprise. The contract at Temper that followed was a different kind of work. I was inside the production codebase, on the <span class="nb">design-token</span> architecture and the checks that enforce it.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="signoff">
    <p class="stance">I am most useful to teams whose product is technically complex and whose interaction model is still being worked out.</p>
    <p>Architecture taught me to decide what the parts are and what each is allowed to do; on an agent product that is most of the job. If that is your product, write to me at the address below.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Sheet>
